/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/secure-context.mem:52:The move that dissolves the wall: ''split the two concerns.'' AUTHENTICATION (who may sync) stays on ''device keys'': each device mints its own keypair, and the built `device-admit/v1` path accepts one founder PersonaGroup root signature. The Tailnet-Lock shape — physical co-presence human-gating admission, ≥2 household devices co-signing so no single device stands as the trust root, and a household-visible, instantly revocable join event on every admit — stands UNBUILT. TLS (the padlock + the secure-context boot) rides a ''separate real cert''. They compose: device-key TOFU for who-syncs, a publicly-trusted cert for the browser's trust store, and ''the family installs nothing''.
