/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/first-realm-arc.mem:57:> ''Name what the founding actually produces, so nobody later reads it as more.'' Three PersonaGroups held by ONE human means one locus of cost at both ends of every hold. The gauge reads that realm ''nominal'' — Ψ ≈ 0, no non-aggregativity, a realm that can act alone against what it holds — and reads it correctly. That costs nothing, because ''the gauge lifts and the lift EXPIRES'': the declaration carries the floor, depth accrues later, and an unrenewed standing lapses without anyone striking it. A founding that gauged deep on day one would name a broken instrument.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/first-realm-arc.mem:67:''④ A second operator founds their own.'' Same rite, their own hearth, their own PersonaGroups, their own charter. ''Independent genesis'' — no shared root, no descent from the first Nexus, and rejoining the mesh later reads as ''RECOGNITION of a foreign chain'', never reconciliation of a forked one (`identity-enacts-relation`).
