/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture.mem:73:* ''WHO axis (read · pledge-gated)'' — the veil and its handles, each step entered by a pledge a member vouches: <<~ scale who "anon-veil -> PersonaGroup-Handle -> CabalGroup-Circle">>. Read-scope rides this axis alone (#/social-axis).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture.mem:216:One operator, N device-vessels. The `PersonaGroup`, a Keyhive group, proves which vessels speak for the same operator. The group faces the mesh ''veiled'' — anon by default, a first-class veil, not a deficit (see the veil doctrine at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity#/the-veil">>). The fleet-join ceremony transfers one face's membership out-of-band (QR, file, direct message) — no server participates.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture.mem:267:''The carriage gate: the subject presents its admit.'' The subject PRESENTS its admit at the wire, quorum-signed by its Nexus; the carrier's contract-in names the NEXUS, so a daemon holds a SET of carried Nexus ids (one contract-in per Nexus); and the gate (`packages/lararium-node/src/nexus-carriage.ts`) checks the presented admit against that set, the carriage board's counted revokes and the kapae antigen (`blocked{}`), and folds no allow roster (`kahu.mem` `#/nexus-scale`, `membership-doctrine.mem` `#/the-operator-contract`). The carriage board itself stands as the antigen's ALLOW-twin — carriers' contracts, roll anchors, hosting acts — and the gate reads it for its revokes alone. The parts: `verifyPresentedAdmit`, the wire's `presentedAdmit`, the carried set (`carried-set.ts`), and the subject stamp signing with a leaf in the NEXUS scope domain (`nexusScopeIndex`), since an admit signed with the PersonaGroup ROOT correlates a human across Nexuses. `foldCarriageSet` (`carriage-registry.ts`) survives as the reading `lares nexus members list` prints, never as the gate.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture.mem:492:* ''Admin-sync gate'' (SOCIAL · WHO, admin scope) — the `PersonaGroup` sentinel: same-operator vessels only.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture.mem:501:* ''anon → walking'' — the ''invite'': any member face (a Kahu, a Lamplighter, another user) hands a burned-once invite, and the spore boots onto the road — no quorum, no board trace, hospitality rather than admission (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-three-admissions">>). A realm's own JOIN rides apart: a held face ''vouches'' and stakes its own standing, which decays if the joiner sours (the siege-gate `rb>c`, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity#/the-siege-gate">>); and a fleet-join `device-admit/v1` edge binds one human's own instruments into their PersonaGroup, never a second human (#/social-axis). ''No invite → anergy:'' the spore draws no ban, it ''stays anon at the floor'', free to re-present later with an invite.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture.mem:504:''The keystone (PROPOSED, unbuilt):'' a ''tiered verdict in the keyholder worker'' — the gate reads the dialing spore and returns one of ''veil · PersonaGroup · owner'', routing each crossing to its right door (the split-gate made operational). The earlier single DENIED verdict read as a fused gate; the tiered verdict dissolves it. the matrix stands ruled; the tiered keyholder-worker verdict awaits build and witness.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture.mem:512:* ''SOCIAL admin-sync door'' — same-operator vessels join through the fleet-join PersonaGroup edge (full private sync); a cross-operator hearth joins by a quorum-signed carriage contract, never the admin door (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine">>). Two sovereign hearths on one LAN CONTRACT; they never merge.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store.mem:357:* ''A removal that leaves out the founding vessel'': the vessel that founded a face's key group holds that group through an identity no device edge names, so a raise over it names no seat a roll can leave out, and it keeps receiving keys. The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, so any other seat's revocation rolls every bag the group reaches; the founder's seat stands upstream of every hand and leaves only by a fresh group (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>; roadmap loop `K12`).
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger.mem:161:''What a herm already carries.'' An envelope holds an open `kind` and an opaque payload, and the relay routes it between proven keys (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/membership-channel.ts`). Two siblings under one PersonaGroup hold a sealed session across a herm (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/sibling-channel.ts`). Either could carry an ask with no change to the frame a herm routes. Neither gives the ask a meaning, a reader at the vessel, or an authority; and a herm sends nothing back when it hands a frame onward.
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-wave-d/wt/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger.mem:165:# ''The asker's proof: the sealed sibling session.'' The ask rides the sealed sibling session, which already proved its far end, and the vessel reads that session's proof as the asker's. A herm's stamp never serves. Reach therefore narrows to one PersonaGroup: an asker outside the vessel's own PersonaGroup holds no such session and asks across no herm.
