    50	
    51	- There are **two different artifacts**, and conflating them is the first mistake. A *petname edge* is a bare key→value entry in an Automerge document's own top-level map. A *DNS binding* is a signed certificate + attached evidence. They are deliberately not the same shape. [design/anchors.md](https://github.com/inkandswitch/onomancy/blob/main/design/anchors.md)
    52	- **Petname edge**: the namestore is "a document's **own top-level map**, not a container within it" — flat, string-keyed, multi-segment keys like `"foo/bar/baz"`, values are **bare Automerge URLs**. No wrapping record, no metadata, no `met_as` field. [specs/path-resolution.md](https://github.com/inkandswitch/onomancy/blob/main/specs/path-resolution.md), [specs/anchoring/petname-anchor.md](https://github.com/inkandswitch/onomancy/blob/main/specs/anchoring/petname-anchor.md)
