   166	
   167	- **Two codecs, not one.** The sedimentree/subduction path is the hand-rolled canonical binary codec: 4-byte schema header `[prefix0, prefix1, type_byte, version]`, prefixes `ST` (sedimentree) / `SU` (subduction); big-endian; **bijou64** bijective varints; **sorted, duplicate-free arrays** whose decoders reject unsorted input; **no optional fields or defaults**; "Decoders reject messages with unknown prefixes or unsupported versions." Signature covers everything before it: schema ‖ IssuerVK ‖ fields. Rejecting CBOR is explicit — "No CBOR/MessagePack edge cases or implementation variance." [design/protocol.md](https://github.com/inkandswitch/subduction/blob/main/design/protocol.md)
